        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "identifiability geometry. In particular, the HERA Pareto envelope shows a knee and does not approach the origin, indicating that single-epoch low-rank cleaning is structurally non-identifiable rather than merely under-tuned. The Pareto projection for HERA (Figure 5b) should be compared directly with the synthetic Pareto panels in Figure 4: both exhibit the same qualitative structure—a nonzero error floor and a knee that prevents the operating point from reaching the origin—confirming that the non-identifiability is not an artifact of the synthetic setup.",
            "block_bbox": [
